formatted_question:
In the paper "FlashAttention-3: Fast and Accurate Attention with Asynchrony and Low-precision", in the single-head attention computation where $\mathbf{S} = \alpha \mathbf{Q}\mathbf{K}^\top$ and $\mathbf{P} = \mathrm{softmax}(\mathbf{S})$, what is the scaling factor $\alpha$ typically set to?
(A) 1/\sqrt{d}.
(B) \sqrt{d}
(C) 1/d
(D) 1/\sqrt{N}
(E) 1/\sqrt{\mathrm{fan\_in}}

raw_knowledge_statement:
Then the attention output $\mathbf{O}$ is computed as:

\begin{equation*}
  \mathbf{S} = \alpha \mathbf{Q} \mathbf{K}^\top \in \mathbb{R}^{N \times N}, \quad \mathbf{P} = \mathrm{softmax}(\mathbf{S}) \in \mathbb{R}^{N \times N}, \quad \mathbf{O} = \mathbf{P}\mathbf{V} \in \mathbb{R}^{N \times d},
\end{equation*}

where $\mathrm{softmax}$ is applied row-wise and one typically sets $\alpha = 1/\sqrt{d}$ as the scaling factor.

formatted_question:
According to the paper "FlashAttention-3: Fast and Accurate Attention with Asynchrony and Low-precision", in the single-head attention formulation where $\mathbf{Q}, \mathbf{K}, \mathbf{V}$ denote the query, key, and value input sequences for a head, what space do these sequences belong to?
(A) \mathbb{R}^{N \times d}.
(B) \mathbb{R}^{N \times N}
(C) \mathbb{R}^{d \times N}
(D) \mathbb{R}^{N \times d_{\mathrm{model}}}
(E) \mathbb{R}^{B \times N \times d}

According to the paper "FlashAttention-3: Fast and Accurate Attention with Asynchrony and Low-precision", in the backward pass of multi-head attention, given the output gradient $\mathbf{dO} \in \mathbb{R}^{N \times d}$, what expression is used to compute $\mathbf{dV}$?
(A) \mathbf{P}\mathbf{dO}
(B) \alpha\mathbf{dS}^\top\mathbf{Q}
(C) \mathbf{P}^\top \mathbf{dO}.
(D) \mathbf{dO}\odot\mathbf{V}
(E) \mathbf{dO}\mathbf{V}^\top

According to the paper "FlashAttention-3: Fast and Accurate Attention with Asynchrony and Low-precision", what is the shape of $\mathbf{Q}_i$ in the requirements of the FlashAttention-3 forward pass without intra-consumer overlapping — CTA view algorithm?
(A) \mathbb{R}^{B_c \times d}
(B) \mathbb{R}^{d \times B_r}
(C) \mathbb{R}^{N \times d}
(D) \mathbb{R}^{B \times B_r \times d}
(E) \mathbb{R}^{B_r \times d}.

According to the paper "FlashAttention-3: Fast and Accurate Attention with Asynchrony and Low-precision", in the consumer warpgroup forward pass, what is the shape of the matrix $\mathbf{Q}_i$ in the requirement that $\mathbf{Q}_i$, $\mathbf{K}$, and $\mathbf{V}$ are matrices in HBM?
(A) \mathbb{R}^{B_r \times B_c}
(B) \mathbb{R}^{d \times B_r}
(C) \mathbb{R}^{N \times d}
(D) \mathbb{R}^{B_c \times d}
(E) \mathbb{R}^{B_r \times d}.

According to the paper "FlashAttention-3: Fast and Accurate Attention with Asynchrony and Low-precision", in the epilogue of the \cref{alg:flash3_wgmma} algorithm after waiting for $\mathbf{V}_{T_c - 1}$ to be loaded in shared memory, what term is added to $\mathbf{O}_{i}$ using WGMMA?
(A) \tilde{\mathbf{P}}_{\mathrm{cur}} \, \mathbf{V}_{T_c - 1}
(B) \tilde{\mathbf{P}}_{\mathrm{last}} \, \mathbf{V}_{T_c - 2}
(C) \tilde{\mathbf{P}}_{\mathrm{next}} \, \mathbf{V}_{T_c - 1}
(D) \operatorname{softmax}(\mathbf{Q}_i \mathbf{K}_{T_c-1}^T) \, \mathbf{V}_{T_c - 1}
(E) \tilde{\mathbf{P}}_{\mathrm{last}} \mathbf{V}_{T_c - 1}.

raw_knowledge_statement:
Since $\mathbf{M}$ is orthogonal, $\mathbf{M} \mathbf{M}^\top = I$ and so $(\mathbf{Q} \mathbf{M}) (\mathbf{K}
  \mathbf{M})^\top = \mathbf{Q} \mathbf{K}^\top$, i.e., multiplying both $\mathbf{Q}$ and $\mathbf{K}$ with
  $\mathbf{M}$ does not change the attention output.

Since $\mathbf{M}$ is orthogonal, $\mathbf{M} \mathbf{M}^\top = I$ and so $(\mathbf{Q} \mathbf{M}) (\mathbf{K}
  \mathbf{M})^\top = \mathbf{Q} \mathbf{K}^\top$, i.e., multiplying both $\mathbf{Q}$ and $\mathbf{K}$ with
  $\mathbf{M}$ does not change the attention output.

To simulate outlier features and activations in LLMs~\citep{dettmers2208llm,
  sun2024massive}, we generate the entries of $\mathbf{Q}, \mathbf{K}, \mathbf{V}$ with the following distribution:

\begin{equation*}
  \mathcal{N}(0, 1) + \mathcal{N}(0, 100) \cdot \mathrm{Bernoulli}(0.001).
\end{equation*}

formatted_question:
In the paper "FlashAttention-3: Fast and Accurate Attention with Asynchrony and Low-precision", in the numerical error comparison against a reference implementation in FP64, which two versions of \textsc{FlashAttention} are evaluated?
(A) \textsc{FlashAttention-2}, \textsc{FlashAttention-3}.
(B) \textsc{FlashAttention-3}, a standard implementation of attention
(C) \textsc{FlashAttention-1}, \textsc{FlashAttention-2}
(D) \textsc{FlashAttention-1}, \textsc{FlashAttention-3}
(E) \textsc{FlashAttention-2}, \textsc{xFormers} memory-efficient attention

According to the paper "FlashAttention-3: Fast and Accurate Attention with Asynchrony and Low-precision", in the ablation study of 2-stage WGMMA-softmax pipelining and warp-specialization for non-causal FP16 \textsc{FlashAttention-3}, what fixed values were used for $\{\text{batch}, \text{seqlen}, \text{nheads}, \text{hdim}\}$?
(A) { 4, 8448, 16, 256}
(B) { 8, 8448, 16, 128}
(C) { 4, 8192, 16, 128}
(D) { 4, 8448, 32, 128}
(E) \{ 4, 8448, 16, 128\}.

