formatted_question:
According to the paper "FlashAttention-3: Fast and Accurate Attention with Asynchrony and Low-precision", what expression do the authors use to compute the FLOPs of the forward pass in their benchmark settings?
(A) 8 \cdot \text{seqlen}^2 \cdot \text{head dimension} \cdot \text{number of heads}
(B) 2 \cdot \text{seqlen}^2 \cdot \text{head dimension} \cdot \text{number of heads}
(C) 4 \cdot \text{seqlen}^2 \cdot \text{head dimension} \cdot \text{number of heads}.
(D) 4 \cdot \text{batch size} \cdot \text{seqlen}^2 \cdot \text{head dimension} \cdot \text{number of heads}
(E) 4 \cdot \text{seqlen} \cdot \text{head dimension} \cdot \text{number of heads}

raw_knowledge_statement:
To calculate the FLOPs of the forward pass, we use:

\begin{equation*}
  4 \cdot \text{seqlen}^2 \cdot \text{head dimension} \cdot \text{number of heads}.
\end{equation*}

Then the attention output $\mathbf{O}$ is computed as:

